        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2001",
        "question_text": "<p>In a <b>voltage-divider bias</b> circuit for a BJT, the base voltage is determined by:</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Voltage-divider bias uses two resistors ($R_1$ and $R_2$) connected in series across the supply voltage ($V_{CC}$). The base voltage ($V_B$) is set by the voltage division between $R_1$ and $R_2$, calculated as $V_B = V_{CC} \times \frac{R_2}{R_1 + R_2}$. This provides stable biasing for the BJT.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
